{"path":"chrono/time_zone/to_sys","title":"std::chrono::time_zone::to_sys","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::chrono::time_zone::</span>to_sys","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/chrono/time_zone/to_sys","section":"chrono","kind":"page","summary":"Converts the local_time tp in this time zone to the corresponding sys_time.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Duration <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> to_sys<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/local_t\"><span class=\"kw2638\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">local_time</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Duration<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> tp <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/system_clock\"><span class=\"kw2641\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">sys_time</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/common_type\"><span class=\"kw641\">std::<span class=\"me2\">common_type_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Duration, <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/duration\"><span class=\"kw1001\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">seconds</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Duration <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> to_sys<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/local_t\"><span class=\"kw2638\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">local_time</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Duration<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> tp, <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/choose\"><span class=\"kw2551\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">choose</span></span></a> z <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/system_clock\"><span class=\"kw2641\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">sys_time</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/common_type\"><span class=\"kw641\">std::<span class=\"me2\">common_type_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Duration, <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/duration\"><span class=\"kw1001\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">seconds</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Converts the <span class=\"t-lc\">local_time</span> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">tp</span></code> in this time zone to the corresponding <span class=\"t-lc\">sys_time</span>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Throws an exception if the conversion is ambiguous or if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">tp</span></code> represents a nonexistent time.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Resolves ambiguity according to the value of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code>:\n<ul><li>If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">choose</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">earliest</span></span></code>, returns the earlier <code>sys_time</code>.\n</li><li>If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">choose</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">latest</span></span></code>, returns the later <code>sys_time</code>.</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\"></span> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">tp</span></code> represents a nonexistent time between two UTC <code>time_point</code>s, those two <code>time_point</code>s will be the same, and that <code>time_point</code> will be returned.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>The UTC equivalent of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">tp</span></code> according to the rules of this time zone.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Throws:\n<ul><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/ambiguous_local_time\"><span class=\"kw2548\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">ambiguous_local_time</span></span></a></span></code> if the conversion is ambiguous,\n</li><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/nonexistent_local_time\"><span class=\"kw2549\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">nonexistent_local_time</span></span></a></span></code> if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">tp</span></code> represents a nonexistent time.</li></ul></div>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>The precision of the result is at least <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/duration\">std::chrono::seconds</a></span>, and will be finer if the argument has finer precision.\n</p><p>Ambiguous and nonexistent local times can occur as a result of time zone transitions (such as daylight saving time). For example, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"st0\">\"2016-03-13 02:30:00\"</span></span></code> does not exist in the <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"st0\">\"America/New_York\"</span></span></code> time zone, while <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"st0\">\"2016-11-06 01:30:00\"</span></span></code> in that time zone can correspond to two UTC time points: <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"nu0\">2016</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">11</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu8\">06</span> <span class=\"nu8\">05</span><span class=\"sy4\">:</span><span class=\"nu0\">30</span><span class=\"sy4\">:</span><span class=\"nu8\">00</span> UTC</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"nu0\">2016</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">11</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu8\">06</span> <span class=\"nu8\">06</span><span class=\"sy4\">:</span><span class=\"nu0\">30</span><span class=\"sy4\">:</span><span class=\"nu8\">00</span> UTC</span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"chrono","title":"Date and time utilities"},{"path":"chrono/time_zone","title":"std::chrono::time_zone"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::chrono::time_zone::to_sys","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++20. Converts the local_time tp in this time zone to the corresponding sys_time."},{"label":"Return value","note":"The UTC equivalent of tp according to the rules of this time zone."},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"Throws: std::chrono::ambiguous_local_time if the conversion is ambiguous, std::chrono::nonexistent_local_time if tp represents a nonexistent time."},{"label":"Notes","note":"The precision of the result is at least std::chrono::seconds, and will be finer if the argument has finer precision."},{"label":"Example"}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":220,"codeBlockCount":0}
